{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDerivExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQExtDerivExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.TrivialWitness"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQExtDeriv.exists","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv-exists.lean#L24-L47","doc":"**Existence of the categorical q-exterior derivative.** Was the axiom\n`CategoricalQExtDeriv.exists_axiom`; proved 2026-11-15 (bean `qou-n2un`).\n\nWitness: the Frobenius–Hopf object at the tensor unit\n(`QOU.TrivialWitness.unitFrobHopf`, which exists in every braided monoidal\ncategory), with `d = π_V = 𝟙` and `q = q⁻¹ = 1`.\n\n**Scope.** This shows the structure is inhabited in every braided monoidal\ncategory, so the former axiom was consistent. It also shows existence is\ncheap: `CategoricalQExtDeriv` places no law on `d` (no `d ≫ d = 0`, no\nLeibniz rule) and no compatibility between `π_V` and `d`, so it does not\npin down a q-exterior derivative. A non-trivial `d_q` needs those laws in\nthe structure. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-q-ext-deriv-exists","label":"prop:categorical-q-ext-deriv-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-ext-deriv-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}